IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) -- baseline-2026-11, shared helpers: day counting and the penalty unit.
--
-- The only module in this encoding that imports daydate (the other modules import this one). Nothing here is a
-- question; the questions are in fwa2-pay.l4, fwa2-protections.l4, fwa2-orders.l4 and fwa2-remedies.l4.
--
-- Edition: Fair Work Act 2009, Compilation No. 73 (register id C2026C00355), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2009A00028.txt; Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA (register id C2026C00368), as deposited at
-- ../../../crimes-act-1914/registers/source-bundle/; Crimes (Amount of a Penalty Unit) Instrument 2026 (F2026N00424), as
-- deposited at ../../../crimes-amount-of-a-penalty-unit-instrument-2026/registers/source-bundle/F2026N00424.txt.

§ `Shared helpers`

-- "Within N days after" a day: the day itself is not counted, so the last day is that day plus N (the reading the Acts
-- Interpretation Act 1901 s 36 gives; that Act is not deposited here, so this is a reading, recorded in NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `number of days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day that is` MEANS Date (Day `the day` PLUS `number of days`)

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `number of months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day some months after` MEANS `add months` `the day` `number of months`

GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `falls on or before` IF Day `first` AT MOST Day `second`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- s 12: "penalty unit has the meaning given by section 4AA of the Crimes Act 1914." Crimes Act s 4AA(1): "$330 (subject
-- to indexation under subsection (3))"; s 4AA(3): indexed "On 1 July 2026 and each third 1 July following"; s 4AA(8):
-- the increased amount "only applies to offences committed on or after the indexation day". The Crimes (Amount of a
-- Penalty Unit) Instrument 2026, s 5: "the amount of a penalty unit is $364", from 1 July 2026.
-- READING: the $364 is applied to civil remedy contraventions as well as offences, by the date of the conduct (s 4AA(8)
-- speaks only of offences; NOTES.md finding 6). Before 1 July 2026 the answer is NOTHING: the deposited compilation
-- gives $330 as the base but not the day from which $330 applied.
GIVEN `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the dollar value of a penalty unit for conduct on` MEANS
    IF `falls on or before` (Date 1 7 2026) `the day of the conduct`
    THEN JUST 364
    ELSE NOTHING
